Square brackets can construct an ordered collection or a String. Read the receiving type alongside the expression to see which result the program asks for.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    scores = [10, 20, 30]
    title = ["Build", " log"]
    tags [String] = ["Build", "log"]
    empty ~[I32] = []
]

`scores` holds three integers. `title` joins two Strings into `"Build log"`,
while `tags` keeps two separate Strings. Give an empty construction a type.
Read or update an element with methods such as `get` and `set`. Indices start at zero.
